cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use anerp or its evaluation results in research, please cite it as below."
title: "anerp: an agent-native headless ERP kernel"
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-16
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Paulpandian-ai/headless-erp"
url: "https://github.com/Paulpandian-ai/headless-erp"
# doi: filled in from the Zenodo record minted for the v0.2.0 GitHub release
abstract: >
  A headless ERP kernel with no user interface whose only public surface is a set of
  typed business-operation tools over the Model Context Protocol and a task-level agent
  over the Agent-to-Agent protocol. Every write is two-phase (simulate/commit), idempotent,
  receipted, policy-checked and event-emitting, on a single double-entry ledger. Built to
  test whether an ERP designed for agents yields higher agent task success and safety than
  a UI-era ERP with an MCP wrapper. Release 0.2.0 includes the evaluation harness and the
  tier-matched matrix results (claude-sonnet-5, gpt-5.6-terra, gemini-3.8-flash; two tool
  surfaces; twenty tasks; three runs) described in REPRODUCIBILITY.md.
authors:
  - name: "anerp contributors"
keywords:
  - ERP
  - agents
  - MCP
  - A2A
  - double-entry ledger
  - evaluation
